From af5cc7198da65caaffbbac56518f6bfa4c27bfab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:22:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] backends/monitor: Expose configured and effective targets
 on D-Bus
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add per-monitor properties to org.gnome.Mutter.DisplayConfig:
GetCurrentState reports the configured "target-peak-luminance",
"target-min-luminance" and "hdr-gamut-source" when set, and the
effective "target-luminance" and "target-primaries" with the provenance
of each, taken from the applied color device and its shared provenance
table. Effective values are only present for active monitors with an
initialized color state.

ApplyMonitorsConfig accepts the same three configured properties. They
replace the previous declaration; omitted fields reset it. Types,
duplicates, enums and ranges are checked before anything changes, so
an invalid request is rejected as a whole, and VERIFY only validates.

Add D-Bus tests for VERIFY, invalid input, a 400 cd/m² user target at a
scaled reference white, and the rejection of a persistent configuration
and its restore. The restore test holds the confirmation the way a
user who has not answered yet would (the test shell otherwise accepts
the configuration immediately), rejects it, waits for the restored peak
with a 10 second bound instead of looping on restore_config_id, and
checks that no restore handle is left behind.

Link: TBD-MR
